c++/reflection: compare dependent splice types structurally

A dependent splice type (SPLICE_SCOPE) was never equal to another
SPLICE_SCOPE node: each node was its own TYPE_CANONICAL and
structural_comptypes had no case for it.  So two declarations of the same
entity that use [: ^^T :] were not recognized as the same, e.g. an alias
template merged from the global module fragments of two modules
("conflicting imported declaration"), or a function template redeclaration.

gcc/cp/ChangeLog:

	* reflect.cc (make_splice_scope): Set TYPE_STRUCTURAL_EQUALITY.
	* typeck.cc (structural_comptypes) <case SPLICE_SCOPE>: New.  Compare
	SPLICE_SCOPE_TYPE_P and SPLICE_SCOPE_EXPR.

Diff is against gcc-17-20261122 (reflect.cc additionally carries an
unrelated one-line local change near line 3924, not part of this diff).
Apply with patch -p1 from the top of the source tree.

--- a/gcc/cp/reflect.cc
+++ b/gcc/cp/reflect.cc
@@ -9529,6 +9529,10 @@ make_splice_scope (tree expr, bool type_
   tree t = cxx_make_type (SPLICE_SCOPE);
   SPLICE_SCOPE_EXPR (t) = expr;
   SPLICE_SCOPE_TYPE_P (t) = type_p;
+  /* Each SPLICE_SCOPE is a new node, so two of them that denote the same
+     type have to be compared by their operands (structural_comptypes),
+     not by TYPE_CANONICAL.  */
+  SET_TYPE_STRUCTURAL_EQUALITY (t);
   return t;
 }
 
--- a/gcc/cp/typeck.cc
+++ b/gcc/cp/typeck.cc
@@ -1674,6 +1674,15 @@ structural_comptypes (tree t1, tree t2,
 	return false;
       break;
 
+    case SPLICE_SCOPE:
+      /* Two dependent splices are the same type (or scope) if their
+	 splice-specifiers are equivalent.  */
+      if (SPLICE_SCOPE_TYPE_P (t1) != SPLICE_SCOPE_TYPE_P (t2))
+	return false;
+      if (!cp_tree_equal (SPLICE_SCOPE_EXPR (t1), SPLICE_SCOPE_EXPR (t2)))
+	return false;
+      break;
+
     default:
       return false;
     }
